Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:59:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] macOS: Level Zero sysman over IntelXe.kext (the device's
 sysfs answered from the kext)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sysman (zesInit, and the SYCL runtime's queries through it) failed on
macOS: LinuxSysmanImp::init names its device from /proc/<pid>/fd and
finds it under /sys/class/drm, and neither exists, so zesInit returned
ZE_RESULT_ERROR_UNINITIALIZED. Every procfs, sysfs and hwmon access of
the Linux sysman goes through NEO::SysCalls, so, as for the render
node, the macOS SysCalls answer those paths: sysfs_macos.cpp keeps a
small read-only tree of the files Linux xe has for the device, filled
from the kext through xemac (xemac_pci_info; xemac_sensors, which reads
the kext's debug.intelxe.sensors_raw sysctl):

  /proc/<pid>/fd/<xemac fd> -> /dev/dri/renderD128
  /sys/class/drm/{card0,renderD128}, /sys/bus/pci/devices/<bdf>,
  /sys/dev/char/226:128 -> /sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:01.0/<bdf>
  <dev>/vendor, device, subsystem_vendor, subsystem_device, revision
  <dev>/tile0/gt0/freq0/{act,cur,rp0,rpn,rpe,min,max}_freq (MHz)
  <dev>/hwmon/hwmon0/name ("xe"), energy1/2_input (uJ),
      temp2/3_input (m°C), power1/2_max and _cap (uW, 0 when the limit
      is off), power1_crit (uW) or curr1_crit (mA)

so the Linux sysman runs unchanged: frequency (GPU domain: hardware
range, SLPC's range, request, actual, efficient), power (card and
package energy counters, PL1/PL2/I1 limits), temperature (GPU =
package, memory = VRAM), memory state (from the xe memory-region query,
as before), PCI address. Everything is read only: a write fails with
ENOENT, which sysman reports as ZE_RESULT_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE
(zesFrequencySetRange, zesPowerSetLimits*); the kext has no live range
or limit control. Not in the tree, so no handle or
UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE/NOT_AVAILABLE: throttle reasons, the media GT,
engine activity (Linux: the xe PMU), PMT telemetry, PCI link speed,
BARs and counters, processes (/proc), standby, schedulers, firmware,
RAS, fans. A file exists when the kext reported its quantity in the
first sample; every read takes a new one. NEO_MACOS_SYSFS_TRACE=1 logs
every path asked.

Directory::getFiles lists directories through SysCalls on macOS too,
so the core finds the device's sysfs directory and reads max_freq:
zeDeviceGetProperties' coreClockRate (SYCL max_clock_frequency) is
RP0 or slpc_max instead of 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
